.SS "\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP setAnchorA (\fBPoint\fP anchor)"

.PP
Move the connection point on body A\&. Pin, slide, pivot and spring constraints support this setter\&. For a groove, use \fBsetGroove()\fP instead\&. Other constraint types throw\&. Finite coordinates are required; invalid input leaves the constraint unchanged\&. Only this endpoint changes\&. See \fBsetAnchors()\fP for solver timing, geometry and lifetime behavior\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIanchor\fP New point in body A's unscaled local distance units; copied\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This constraint for chaining\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBgetAnchorA()\fP, \fBsetAnchors()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP setAnchorB (\fBPoint\fP anchor)"

.PP
Move the connection point on body B\&. Pin, slide, pivot, groove and spring constraints support this setter\&. Other constraint types throw\&. Finite coordinates are required; invalid input leaves the constraint unchanged\&. Only this endpoint changes\&. See \fBsetAnchors()\fP for solver timing, geometry and lifetime behavior\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIanchor\fP New point in body B's unscaled local distance units; copied\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This constraint for chaining\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBgetAnchorB()\fP, \fBsetAnchors()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP setAnchors (\fBPoint\fP anchorA, \fBPoint\fP anchorB)"

.PP
Move both connection points atomically\&. Supports pin, slide, pivot and spring constraints\&. Groove and angular-only constraints throw\&. Both Points must have finite coordinates\&. Validation occurs before either stored point changes; getters report successful edits immediately\&.

.PP
The next physics step uses the new anchors\&. This includes edits requested in a collision callback: the active solver joint is not mutated during that solve\&. Connected sleeping bodies wake when the edit reaches the native solver\&. Repeating the same coordinates does not restart the joint\&. The public constraint handle, body endpoints, force/break limits and collision policy are preserved\&.

.PP
Moving anchors does not teleport bodies, change velocities, resize colliders, recalculate mass/inertia, or change a pin's distance, slide limits or spring rest length\&. The solver may move bodies to satisfy the new geometry\&. Edited anchors are saved in scene snapshots, including edits made before the next solve\&. A retained disconnected constraint stays editable but is not reconnected\&.

.PP
This edits physical connection points, not animation bones or \fBPart\fP offsets\&. Physical \fBPart\fP IK continues to validate its joint geometry against its \fBPart\fP chain; incompatible anchors produce a controller error instead of silently moving its captured chain offsets\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIanchorA\fP New point in body A's unscaled local distance units; copied\&. 
.br
\fIanchorB\fP New point in body B's unscaled local distance units; copied\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This constraint for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
The example assumes upperArm and forearm are Parts with physics bodies in the same layer, with millimeters as the application's distance unit\&. The coordinates are relative to each body's origin\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const elbow = upperArm\&.physics\&.createPivotJoint(forearm\&.physics,
    new pdg\&.Point(0, 150), new pdg\&.Point(0, \-130));
elbow\&.setAnchors(new pdg\&.Point(0, 145), new pdg\&.Point(0, \-125));

.fi
.PP
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBgetAnchorA()\fP, \fBgetAnchorB()\fP, \fBsetAnchorA()\fP, \fBsetAnchorB()\fP, \fBsetGroove()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP setAngleLimits (number minAngle, number maxAngle)"

.PP
Change both bounds of a rotary-limit constraint\&. Both bounds must be finite and ordered; equal values lock the relative angle\&. Invalid input leaves both old bounds intact\&. Other constraint types throw\&. Getters and linked \fBPart\fP IK see the change immediately\&. Both physics solvers apply it on the next constraint step\&. This does not teleport either body or reconnect a disconnected constraint\&. The physical interval may span multiple turns; \fBPart\fP IK links accept at most one turn and report an error for a wider interval\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIminAngle\fP Minimum body B rotation relative to A, in radians\&. 
.br
\fImaxAngle\fP Maximum body B rotation relative to A, in radians\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This constraint for chaining\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBgetMinAngle()\fP, \fBgetMaxAngle()\fP, \fBPart::setIKLimits()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP setBreakForce (number value)"

.PP
Choose the force or torque that breaks this constraint\&. The threshold is checked after each solve against impulse divided by elapsed seconds\&. Breaking disconnects only this constraint, leaving the handle queryable\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIvalue\fP Finite nonnegative threshold; zero disables breaking\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This object, for chaining\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP setCollideBodies (boolean value)"

.PP
Allow contacts between connected endpoints\&. Defaults to false\&. Collision masks, groups and layers still apply when enabled\&. This does not create collision geometry\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIvalue\fP Whether the two bodies may collide\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This object, for chaining\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP setGroove (\fBPoint\fP start, \fBPoint\fP end)"

.PP
Move both endpoints of a groove joint's track atomically\&. Only groove constraints support this setter\&. Coordinates must be finite and the endpoints more than 1e-8 local distance units apart\&. Invalid input leaves both endpoints unchanged\&. Body B's anchor stays unchanged; use \fBsetAnchorB()\fP to edit it\&. Getters report the change immediately; the solver adopts it on the next step\&. The same timing, lifetime and body-state rules as \fBsetAnchors()\fP apply\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIstart\fP New track start in body A's unscaled local distance units; copied\&. 
.br
\fIend\fP New track end in body A's unscaled local distance units; copied\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This constraint for chaining\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBgetGrooveStart()\fP, \fBgetGrooveEnd()\fP, \fBsetAnchorB()\fP, \fBsetAnchors()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP setMaxForce (number value)"

.PP
Set the maximum constraint force or torque\&. Linear constraints use force; angular constraints use torque\&. Takes effect on the next solve\&. Both solvers cap the impulse per step to this value times elapsed seconds\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIvalue\fP Nonnegative maximum, including positive infinity\&. Default is infinity except motors\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This object, for chaining\&. 
.RE
.PP


